---
import GovLayout from '../../layouts/GovLayout.astro';
import PhaseBanner from '../../components/PhaseBanner.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import SummaryBox from '../../components/SummaryBox.astro';
import InsetText from '../../components/InsetText.astro';
import Sidebar from '../../components/Sidebar.astro';
---
<GovLayout title="Money Laundering & Criminal Faction" department="Ministry of Justice" description="Mechanics of the Criminal Faction, illicit cargo, Criminal Records, and how Wanted status works in ASEAN Motor Club.">

<PhaseBanner tag="Policy" text="Updated 7 April 2026" />
<Breadcrumbs items={[
  { label: "Justice & Law Enforcement", href: "/justice" },
  { label: "Money Laundering & Criminal Faction", href: "/justice/money-laundering" },
]} />

<main class="govuk-main-wrapper">
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <h1>Money Laundering &amp; Criminal Faction</h1>

      <SummaryBox title="Summary">
        <p>Delivering illicit cargo creates an active <strong>Criminal Record</strong> — the single source of truth for your criminal status. Your record tracks two amounts: a permanent <strong>total</strong> and a <strong>confiscatable amount</strong> that decays over time while you are online. Upon arrest, police confiscate your Wanted bounty plus your remaining confiscatable amount, and your Criminal Record is cleared.</p>
      </SummaryBox>

      <h2 id="illicit-cargo">1. Illicit Cargo</h2>
      <p>The following cargo types are considered illicit and trigger criminal mechanics on delivery:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Money / Money Pallet</li>
        <li>Ganja / Ganja Pallet</li>
        <li>Coca Leaves Pallet</li>
        <li>Cocaine</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="criminal-record">2. Criminal Record</h2>
      <p>Your first illicit delivery creates an active <strong>Criminal Record</strong> and immediately adds the <code>[C]</code> tag to your in-game name. The Criminal Record persists indefinitely — it is only cleared when you are arrested.</p>

      <h3>Two tracked amounts</h3>
      <p>Each Criminal Record tracks two separate values:</p>
      <table class="govuk-table">
        <caption>Criminal Record fields</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Total amount</strong></td>
            <td>The permanent lifetime sum of all illicit delivery payments linked to this record. Never decreases. Used for criminal level display.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Confiscatable amount</strong></td>
            <td>Also accumulates with each delivery, but <strong>decays over time</strong> while you are online. This is the amount at risk of confiscation on arrest. Shown in <code>/wanted</code>.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h3>Confiscatable amount decay</h3>
      <p>The confiscatable amount decays exponentially every minute — but <strong>only while you are online</strong>. Logging off pauses the decay entirely. Amounts below <strong>$100</strong> are rounded down to zero.</p>
      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Confiscatable amount decay</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Time online</th><th>Fraction remaining</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">0 minutes</td><td>100%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">1 hour</td><td>~87%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">4 hours</td><td>50% (half-life)</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">8 hours</td><td>25%</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">24 hours</td><td>~1.6%</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <InsetText>
        The decay only ticks while you are in-game. Staying offline effectively freezes your confiscatable amount at its current value indefinitely.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="criminal-level">3. Criminal Level</h2>
      <p>Your criminal level is based on your <strong>cumulative lifetime laundered total</strong> across all records — it never resets, even after arrest. Your level increases by 1 for every <strong>$50,000 laundered</strong>.</p>
      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Criminal level thresholds</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Cumulative laundered</th><th>Tag</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">1</td><td>$0 – $49,999</td><td><code>[C]</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">2</td><td>$50,000 – $99,999</td><td><code>[C2]</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">3</td><td>$100,000 – $149,999</td><td><code>[C3]</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left"><em>N</em></td><td><em>(N − 1) × $50,000</em> onwards</td><td><code>[C<em>N</em>]</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <InsetText>
        Arrest reduces your laundered total by the confiscatable amount confiscated — not the full lifetime total. Your criminal level may therefore decrease slightly after arrest.
      </InsetText>

      <h2 id="treasury-cost">4. Treasury Cost</h2>
      <p>Money deliveries deduct <strong>20% of the laundered payment</strong> from the public Treasury Fund. Other illicit cargo types (drugs) do not have a treasury cost.</p>

      <h2 id="wanted-trigger">5. Wanted Status Trigger</h2>
      <p>Each illicit delivery has a chance of triggering a <strong>Wanted</strong> status on top of the Criminal Record. The probability scales with delivery value:</p>

      <table class="govuk-table govuk-table--numeric">
        <caption>Wanted trigger probability by delivery value</caption>
        <thead><tr><th>Delivery value</th><th>Wanted chance</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">Any amount</td><td>10% minimum (floor)</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">$100,000 or more</td><td>100% (guaranteed)</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="text-align:left">Between $0 and $100,000</td><td>Linearly interpolated</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <InsetText>
        <strong>30-second debounce window:</strong> Multiple deliveries within 30 seconds of each other are aggregated before the probability roll. Splitting a large delivery into many small ones (e.g. one cargo at a time) is treated identically to a single large delivery.
      </InsetText>

      <p>If a Wanted status is already active, any new delivery refreshes it and adds the payment to the Wanted bounty. See <a href="/justice/arrest-wanted" class="govuk-link">Arrest &amp; Wanted System</a> for full Wanted mechanics.</p>

      <h2 id="arrest-confiscation">6. Arrest &amp; Confiscation</h2>
      <p>When you are arrested, two things happen simultaneously:</p>
      <ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
        <li>Your <strong>Wanted record is expired</strong> and the Wanted bounty (<code>Wanted.amount</code>) is confiscated.</li>
        <li>Your <strong>Criminal Record is cleared</strong> (<code>[C]</code> tag removed) and the <strong>confiscatable amount</strong> from the Criminal Record is also confiscated.</li>
      </ol>

      <p>The <strong>total confiscation</strong> is therefore:</p>
      <p><code>Confiscation = Wanted.amount + CriminalRecord.confiscatable_amount</code></p>

      <InsetText>
        If you have a Criminal Record but no active Wanted status (you were never flagged or already escaped), the confiscatable amount is still seized on arrest — police can arrest you any time while you have a <code>[C]</code> tag.
      </InsetText>

      <h3>After arrest</h3>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>Your Criminal Record is cleared — <code>[C]</code> tag is immediately removed</li>
        <li>Your <strong>criminal laundered total is reduced</strong> by the confiscatable amount seized</li>
        <li>The full confiscated sum is paid to the arresting officer as a reward</li>
        <li>A Confiscation record is permanently created, linking the suspect, officer, and amount</li>
        <li>Your next illicit delivery creates a fresh Criminal Record from zero</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="setwanted-cooldown">7. /setwanted Cooldown</h2>
      <p>After a Wanted status expires (via escape or arrest), police cannot immediately re-target the same player using <code>/setwanted</code>. A <strong>1-hour cooldown</strong> applies from the moment the Wanted record expires. The cooldown timer and remaining minutes are shown in the command reply.</p>

    </div>
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-one-third">
      <Sidebar items={[
        { label: "Illicit Cargo", href: "#illicit-cargo" },
        { label: "Criminal Record", href: "#criminal-record" },
        { label: "Criminal Level", href: "#criminal-level" },
        { label: "Treasury Cost", href: "#treasury-cost" },
        { label: "Wanted Trigger", href: "#wanted-trigger" },
        { label: "Arrest & Confiscation", href: "#arrest-confiscation" },
        { label: "/setwanted Cooldown", href: "#setwanted-cooldown" },
      ]} />
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

</GovLayout>
